# playwright-cli's session artifacts (snapshots, console logs) and its
# local config file -- the config is where a Claude Code sandbox session
# points executablePath at the container's pre-installed browser and
# disables Chromium's sandbox (required running as root in a container),
# neither of which should silently apply to a real contributor's machine.
# See .claude/skills/playwright-cli/NOTICE.md for the config to recreate.
.playwright-cli/
.playwright/

# ruflo (see .claude/hooks/session-start.sh). Contrary to what v1.32 said,
# the plugin path does write into the repo -- not at install time, but the
# moment its hooks fire or a `ruflo` command runs. Three separate paths:
# .claude-flow/ at the root, a proven-config pair under .claude/, and a
# .claude/security-scans/ directory created inside whatever tree you point
# `ruflo security scan` at (backend/src/, in our case). All of it is local
# tooling state -- policy weights, scan output -- that is regenerated on
# demand and means nothing to another checkout, so none of it belongs in
# git. Ignored rather than deleted so the tooling keeps working.
.claude-flow/
.claude/proven-config.json
.claude/.proven-config-version
**/.claude/security-scans/
